WEBVTT

00:01.530 --> 00:04.670
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.670 --> 00:08.200
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.200 --> 00:16.130
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.320 --> 00:27.960
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.960 --> 00:33.860
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.860 --> 00:42.800
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.800 --> 00:47.510
Like the wind

00:47.510 --> 00:50.580
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.580 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.660
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.660 --> 01:07.400
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.400 --> 01:13.540
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.540 --> 01:20.210
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.210 --> 01:27.510
The roadless journey continues

01:37.890 --> 01:41.290
Ellis... Ellis...

01:44.570 --> 01:46.230
Ellis!

01:48.200 --> 01:50.610
Disappeared?

01:50.610 --> 01:53.040
This isn't like you.

01:53.040 --> 01:56.740
I have a rough idea of where to go.
I'll contact you again later.

02:01.580 --> 02:04.450
Nadie and Ellis have disappeared.

02:06.790 --> 02:08.590
The two...

02:08.590 --> 02:10.420
...were digging.

02:17.600 --> 02:19.590
Take this!

02:24.970 --> 02:26.600
We did it!

02:42.290 --> 02:45.430
- How's it look?
- Still coming.

02:45.430 --> 02:47.300
I screwed this up.

02:47.300 --> 02:50.270
I should've headed for town
instead of trying to be tricky.

02:50.270 --> 02:52.830
Not to mention running out
of ammo at a time like this...

02:52.830 --> 02:54.670
I'm a failure as a bounty hunter.

02:54.670 --> 02:56.640
Nadie's a failure.

02:56.640 --> 02:58.870
Shut up, bounty.

02:58.870 --> 03:02.710
I guess we have no choice
but to keep going straight.

03:02.710 --> 03:05.370
- Let's go.
- Yessir.

03:34.240 --> 03:39.480
I wish they'd make it a crime
to leave outdated maps in cars...

03:39.480 --> 03:43.820
Honestly! Forget ammo, it looks
like we won't even find tacos here.

03:43.820 --> 03:47.990
♪ Taco, taco, tacos! Tasty tacos! ♪

03:47.990 --> 03:53.090
♪ The most awesome tacos are Amigo Tacos! ♪

03:53.090 --> 03:55.660
- You forgot the "teehee."
- Teehee.

03:55.660 --> 03:58.430
Didn't you say you hated that song?

03:58.430 --> 04:01.900
Yup, I hate it.

04:01.900 --> 04:05.710
You get gas, I get water. On the double.

04:05.710 --> 04:08.900
We're getting out of here
before he catches up to us.

04:20.520 --> 04:22.510
A silver mine...

04:24.190 --> 04:26.180
Ooh, found it!

04:34.200 --> 04:37.940
Ow, that hurt...

04:37.940 --> 04:40.070
So it's a dried-up well.

04:42.140 --> 04:46.110
I don't think I can climb out of here on my own.

04:46.110 --> 04:49.880
Ellis! Bring me a rope!

04:58.590 --> 05:00.730
Is this... a door?

05:00.730 --> 05:02.400
Nadie.

05:02.400 --> 05:04.900
I brought it.

05:04.900 --> 05:07.470
What are we going to do
with you down here, too?!

05:07.470 --> 05:09.300
What are we going to do?

05:13.780 --> 05:15.610
That should do it.

05:22.280 --> 05:25.590
- It's not nearly long enough!
- You're right.

05:25.590 --> 05:28.790
It'd make me real happy if
you'd bring me a longer one.

05:28.790 --> 05:30.450
Yessir.

05:32.960 --> 05:36.160
- Oh...
- What's wrong?

05:36.160 --> 05:37.860
He's here.

05:47.380 --> 05:49.380
What're we going to do?!

05:49.380 --> 05:53.980
If he finds us here, we're sitting ducks!

05:53.980 --> 05:56.050
I know!

05:56.050 --> 05:57.880
Just maybe...

06:07.060 --> 06:08.890
Yes!

06:13.840 --> 06:18.970
I don't know who made it,
but I have to say I'm grateful.

06:18.970 --> 06:21.540
Now, if only there was a long
rope or ammo lying around,

06:21.540 --> 06:24.850
that'd be awesome.

06:24.850 --> 06:26.540
What's wrong?

06:29.820 --> 06:32.340
All I wanted was the ammo...

07:03.520 --> 07:05.420
Time to regroup.

07:09.860 --> 07:13.030
You know you still have the safety on?

07:13.030 --> 07:14.520
What?

07:16.430 --> 07:18.630
Ellis, light.

07:18.630 --> 07:20.030
Whoa, that's bright!

07:20.030 --> 07:22.040
Oh, I'm sorry!

07:22.040 --> 07:24.300
Why did you turn the light on?

07:30.310 --> 07:32.710
Didn't you just say "Iris"?

07:32.710 --> 07:34.750
"Ellis"!

07:34.750 --> 07:36.080
Teehee.

07:36.080 --> 07:38.790
Oh, I'm sorry! Then I'll just...

07:38.790 --> 07:41.550
- You don't have to turn it off.
- Y-Yes, ma'am.

07:44.790 --> 07:47.780
I've got a lot of questions, but...

07:49.560 --> 07:52.900
Who are you? And what are you doing here?

07:52.900 --> 07:58.640
Well, my name is Iris Gonzalez and...

07:58.640 --> 08:01.940
...I'm digging for silver!

08:01.940 --> 08:03.810
Pardon?

08:15.960 --> 08:19.360
Wow, so this connects to the silver mine.

08:19.360 --> 08:20.530
Yes.

08:20.530 --> 08:25.300
So, about this scoundrel you
mentioned earlier, who is after you...

08:25.300 --> 08:29.000
We happened to run into him
just when I'd run out of ammo.

08:29.000 --> 08:31.810
And he's been doggedly chasing us since then.

08:31.810 --> 08:36.610
If that's the case, please
take it easy here for a while.

08:42.980 --> 08:47.390
In the past, it seems there were
about 50 people living here.

08:47.390 --> 08:51.630
But now, I am the only one using the facilities.

08:51.630 --> 08:53.460
Here you are.

08:54.900 --> 08:59.500
I get that you really live here.

08:59.500 --> 09:03.400
I also get that you're
apparently digging for silver.

09:03.400 --> 09:07.580
And I, too, get that you two
are apparently not thieves,

09:07.580 --> 09:09.640
so I am relieved.

09:09.640 --> 09:11.150
But you know...

09:11.150 --> 09:15.720
I hate to say this, but hasn't the
silver here been all mined already?

09:15.720 --> 09:17.650
That's why it was closed up, right?

09:17.650 --> 09:19.550
Yes, that's what I've heard.

09:19.550 --> 09:20.990
But you just said...

09:20.990 --> 09:24.360
Oh, I'm sorry. I should've
explained myself more.

09:24.360 --> 09:30.230
What I'm trying to dig up, accurately
speaking, is "the Silver Cross."

09:30.230 --> 09:34.200
The Silver... Cross?

09:34.200 --> 09:36.830
This is a map my father left me.

09:55.960 --> 09:59.730
It was shortly before I was
to graduate from college.

09:59.730 --> 10:01.760
One day, my professor asked me,

10:01.760 --> 10:04.470
"What are you doing after graduation?"

10:04.470 --> 10:10.100
I had never even thought about
what to do after graduation until then.

10:10.100 --> 10:12.710
Because up to that point, once I graduated,

10:12.710 --> 10:15.440
I just had to move on to
the next level of school.

10:15.440 --> 10:17.040
Talk about laid-back.

10:17.040 --> 10:20.580
Other people said they were
going to work for companies,

10:20.580 --> 10:23.050
but that seemed like a tough thing to do.

10:23.050 --> 10:27.050
I wanted to find something I could
grind away at on my own, if possible.

10:27.050 --> 10:32.060
That was when my father gave
me this map and said to me,

10:32.060 --> 10:35.900
"In that case, why don't you try
looking for the Silver Cross?"

10:35.900 --> 10:38.270
And thus, you came all the way out here.

10:38.270 --> 10:40.800
- Yes.
- That's incredible!

10:40.800 --> 10:45.400
It is, right? To be honest,
I think it's incredible, too.

10:48.240 --> 10:50.750
You're really willing to lend me a hand?

10:50.750 --> 10:53.250
Enough to repay you for
the gas and water, at least.

10:53.250 --> 10:54.620
And the tea.

10:54.620 --> 10:57.790
It's not in my nature to accept charity.

10:57.790 --> 11:00.020
Besides...

11:00.020 --> 11:05.020
I want to kill some time here
until that guy moves on.

11:36.790 --> 11:39.630
The Silver Cross was hidden in this mountain

11:39.630 --> 11:41.630
approximately 400 years ago.

11:41.630 --> 11:44.670
But since then, multiple mining operations

11:44.670 --> 11:46.570
have produced numerous tunnels

11:46.570 --> 11:51.210
and none of the places completely
match up with the original map now.

11:51.210 --> 11:52.970
This is practically a maze.

11:52.970 --> 11:54.310
I'm sorry.

11:54.310 --> 11:57.750
Nah, it's nothing you need to apologize for.

11:57.750 --> 12:00.720
So anyway, do you dig in that outfit, too?

12:00.720 --> 12:04.390
What? Oh, I'm sorry.

12:04.390 --> 12:06.090
But my elder sister said

12:06.090 --> 12:09.220
that I should wear clothes I'm
accustomed to when laboring.

12:09.220 --> 12:11.930
This is what I'm most accustomed to

12:11.930 --> 12:15.400
and I have lots of other similar outfits, so...

12:15.400 --> 12:17.160
I see.

12:19.170 --> 12:20.500
Day...

12:20.500 --> 12:22.240
...after day...

12:22.240 --> 12:24.340
Doing this sort of thing...

12:24.340 --> 12:25.740
Don't you get tired of it?

12:25.740 --> 12:27.070
What?

12:27.070 --> 12:30.380
Every day, all you do is dig holes, right?

12:30.380 --> 12:31.910
Don't you get bored?

12:31.910 --> 12:36.380
But back when I was a student,
I did nothing but attend lectures every day,

12:36.380 --> 12:39.450
and I never once thought that it was boring.

12:39.450 --> 12:41.720
You're something else.

12:48.430 --> 12:50.130
Let us take a break.

12:50.130 --> 12:52.360
I'll go bring us some tea.

13:02.140 --> 13:05.980
I don't know whether to
call her earnest or what...

13:10.620 --> 13:12.390
They're similar, but different, I guess.

13:12.390 --> 13:15.320
Both in name and personality.

13:15.320 --> 13:17.060
What's that?

13:17.060 --> 13:20.080
- It's collapsed.
- What? Iris!

13:24.430 --> 13:25.730
Are you okay?

13:25.730 --> 13:29.900
Oh, I'm sorry to have caused you worry.

13:29.900 --> 13:32.670
This is no time to be laid-back
and saying things like that.

13:38.610 --> 13:41.750
Why?

13:41.750 --> 13:46.420
This kind of thing has never happened before.

13:46.420 --> 13:48.260
It's collapsing all over the place.

13:48.260 --> 13:50.120
Really?

13:50.120 --> 13:52.360
Explosions.

13:52.360 --> 13:54.090
It can't be...

14:03.370 --> 14:05.940
Setting off bombs in a place like this...

14:05.940 --> 14:07.880
That idiot.

14:07.880 --> 14:10.440
Sorry. We got you dragged into this.

14:10.440 --> 14:13.450
It looks like he's planning to bury us alive.

14:13.450 --> 14:16.010
Is there some way we could sneak out of here?

14:19.150 --> 14:20.350
Iris?

14:20.350 --> 14:24.060
That's right. I need to
look for the Silver Cross.

14:24.060 --> 14:25.650
Huh?

14:27.060 --> 14:30.120
This is no time to be doing that, now is it?

14:33.530 --> 14:36.040
But... But...

14:36.040 --> 14:40.040
My father did tell me to
look for the Silver Cross,

14:40.040 --> 14:42.570
so I should be good and do as he said.

14:45.910 --> 14:47.410
Calm down.

14:47.410 --> 14:48.880
Do you understand the situation we're in?

14:48.880 --> 14:53.650
Y-Yes. Which is why I will
be calm and I will dig!

14:53.650 --> 14:56.060
"I will dig"?

14:56.060 --> 14:58.250
Don't you have a will of your own?

15:00.030 --> 15:02.000
You're a human being, aren't you?

15:02.000 --> 15:04.330
You're not your father's robot, right?

15:04.330 --> 15:08.560
In which case, you should at least
think for yourself about what to do.

15:12.670 --> 15:14.500
This way.

15:29.190 --> 15:31.190
Come on, Iris, come with us.

15:31.190 --> 15:38.270
And until we get out of here, do as I say.

15:38.270 --> 15:41.270
Got it?

15:41.270 --> 15:43.860
Y-Yes.

15:51.250 --> 15:52.450
Here.

15:52.450 --> 15:54.420
As I recall,

15:54.420 --> 15:58.550
the space between the tunnels
around here is extremely close...

15:58.550 --> 16:01.060
So, that means if we dig, we can get out, right?

16:01.060 --> 16:04.160
Probably...

16:04.160 --> 16:06.330
You help, too.

16:06.330 --> 16:08.960
Yes, I-I'm sorry!

16:24.240 --> 16:26.240
All right, we're through.

16:29.480 --> 16:32.450
Which way?

16:32.450 --> 16:34.180
This way.

16:42.260 --> 16:44.600
Iris, you have your gun, right?

16:44.600 --> 16:46.130
Oh, yes...

16:46.130 --> 16:47.600
Let me have it, just in case.

16:47.600 --> 16:49.000
What?

16:49.000 --> 16:50.940
But my elder brother gave it to me

16:50.940 --> 16:54.270
and told me to keep it
on my person at all times...

16:54.270 --> 16:55.880
Quit arguing with me.

16:55.880 --> 16:58.440
Y-Yes, ma'am.

17:31.210 --> 17:33.680
If you have any last words, say them now.

17:37.350 --> 17:39.750
- Nadie...
- Run!

17:48.030 --> 17:49.830
Nadie, overhead.

17:49.830 --> 17:51.560
Overhead?

17:59.240 --> 18:01.040
Ellis, what's the map say?

18:01.040 --> 18:03.410
Three more centimeters to the exit.

18:03.410 --> 18:05.750
Oh, you would say that.

18:05.750 --> 18:07.740
Oh!

18:16.690 --> 18:19.690
Oh, it's all over!

18:19.690 --> 18:21.960
If only I had listened to my father, after all.

18:21.960 --> 18:24.600
Kept my head down and continued
my search for the Silver Cross...

18:24.600 --> 18:27.800
Uh, no, you'd be dead
already if you'd done that.

18:34.880 --> 18:37.610
Time to dig! Ellis! Iris!

18:44.590 --> 18:46.780
Take this!

18:56.760 --> 18:58.750
This is...

19:05.240 --> 19:07.770
We did it!

19:07.770 --> 19:09.770
We did it...

19:11.910 --> 19:15.940
The Silver... Cross?

19:18.750 --> 19:20.790
I never imagined that it really existed.

19:20.790 --> 19:24.460
I totally thought the map was fake.

19:24.460 --> 19:27.960
Iris, it's the Silver Cross
you've been looking for!

19:27.960 --> 19:29.960
You found it!

19:29.960 --> 19:33.270
R-Right...

19:33.270 --> 19:35.670
You're not happy?

19:35.670 --> 19:39.340
It's times like this when you should
be bursting with happiness, right?

19:39.340 --> 19:42.510
Is it okay... to be happy?

19:42.510 --> 19:43.940
Huh?

19:43.940 --> 19:48.220
Can't you even do something like that
without being told to by others?

19:48.220 --> 19:50.010
Nadie.

19:51.120 --> 19:52.950
It's going to collapse.

19:56.560 --> 19:58.320
Over there!

20:24.890 --> 20:29.220
Aw, and after we'd found the treasure, too...

20:43.900 --> 20:47.340
Say, what are you going to do now?

20:51.380 --> 20:55.120
I guess you can't decide that until
someone tells you what to do...

20:55.120 --> 20:59.220
- I... will remain here.
- What?

20:59.220 --> 21:02.020
It was so very beautiful and large...

21:02.020 --> 21:06.530
People have long been fascinated by silver,

21:06.530 --> 21:09.700
and I think I can finally understand why.

21:09.700 --> 21:11.530
Iris...

21:11.530 --> 21:16.570
I want to remain here and excavate
that cross one more time!

21:16.570 --> 21:19.270
So you're still listening
to what your father said...

21:19.270 --> 21:21.710
My father has nothing to do with it.

21:21.710 --> 21:24.810
This is my own will.

21:24.810 --> 21:29.480
I sincerely wish to make that cross mine.

21:29.480 --> 21:33.980
And this time for sure,
I want to rejoice at my find!

21:36.320 --> 21:38.460
Oh, well.

21:38.460 --> 21:40.660
You do your best, Iris!

21:40.660 --> 21:42.320
I will!

21:47.730 --> 21:51.740
Does it make you happy
to find something you want?

21:51.740 --> 21:54.730
If it's something you truly want.

22:02.350 --> 22:04.280
I see...

22:07.990 --> 22:09.290
Now...

22:09.290 --> 22:11.810
First, I need to go change my clothes.

22:15.200 --> 22:17.530
It's all... in there...

22:20.100 --> 22:22.760
What should I do?

22:26.840 --> 22:31.450
The report that a giant
silver cross was excavated...

22:31.450 --> 22:33.970
...has yet to come in.

22:36.620 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.890
Like flowers that never die

22:43.890 --> 22:47.790
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.790 --> 22:55.960
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.210 --> 23:05.710
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.710 --> 23:11.490
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.490 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.560
A night of red stars

23:19.560 --> 23:23.560
The vanishing warmth

23:23.560 --> 23:27.500
I want to keep it here

23:27.500 --> 23:34.010
You, with your eyes closed

23:34.010 --> 23:37.940
Yearning over and over

23:37.940 --> 23:41.380
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.380 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.790
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.790 --> 23:56.790
...everything
